[stderr] +# Round lifecycle bible
[stderr] +
[stderr] +**Scope:** accepted design evidence for `GAME-005`, `GAME-006`, `GPI-008`, and
[stderr] +`GPI-009`. This defines a future-core contract and fixtures, not production
[stderr] +content or an implementation. All content IDs refer to the frozen package held
[stderr] +by the run; no network response, wall clock, UI ordering, or random source can
[stderr] +alter a fixture result.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## GPI-008 — First Whistle tutorial
[stderr] +
[stderr] +`First Whistle` is a fixed five-card, non-timed onboarding round. It is
[stderr] +available from a new local profile when the installed tutorial package is
[stderr] +present, including offline. It does not need sign-in, a purchase, notifications,
[stderr] +or a remote service. Each card has the indicated one purpose; its final
[stderr] +published wording, answer IDs, provenance, and two reviews are governed by the
[stderr] +question-card and adjudication bibles before it may ship.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +| Position / ID | Fixed format | Instructional purpose | Required resolution and next state |
[stderr] +| --- | --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] +| 1 / `TUT-01` | four-option select | Read the prompt, choose one labelled option, and confirm. | Accepted or rejected select submission resolves the attempt, exposes text feedback, and opens `TUT-02`. |
[stderr] +| 2 / `TUT-02` | short typed answer | Enter a short answer and confirm; only configured canonical text/aliases are accepted. | A typed submission resolves through GAME-003 normalisation, shows canonical answer/explanation if rejected, and opens `TUT-03`. |
[stderr] +| 3 / `TUT-03` | true/false | Recognise that feedback says whether the resolved answer was accepted. | Submission resolves once; feedback is available in text plus non-colour state, then opens `TUT-04`. |
[stderr] +| 4 / `TUT-04` | ordered pair | Inspect the explanation after resolving an answer. | Submission resolves once; explanation is available before continue, then opens `TUT-05`. |
[stderr] +| 5 / `TUT-05` | four-option select | Pause deliberately, confirm that the current safe state is saved, then resume and finish. | Explicit pause commits a snapshot after the unresolved card is displayed; resume restores `TUT-05`; resolved completion commits result and `first_whistle_complete`. |
[stderr] +
[stderr] +The tutorial's card sequence is exactly `[TUT-01, TUT-02, TUT-03, TUT-04,
[stderr] +TUT-05]`; it has no selection seed, repeat filter, timer, skip, or reordering.
[stderr] +The tutorial selection never silently substitutes an unavailable card. If its
[stderr] +fixed package is unavailable or invalid, start is blocked with a plain-language
[stderr] +retry/return-home state.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +### Tutorial deterministic fixtures
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Fixture input includes a frozen `tutorial-v1` package containing the five IDs,
[stderr] +a new local profile, and the stated actions. `resolve` means the matching
[stderr] +GAME-003 fixture supplies an immutable accepted/rejected attempt; the
[stderr] +particular football fact is deliberately not duplicated here.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +| ID | Input / action | Expected deterministic state, record, and visible outcome |
[stderr] +| --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] +| `TUT-FX-01` | Start `tutorial-v1`; resolve `TUT-01`; continue. | Active card changes `TUT-01 → TUT-02`; one immutable TUT-01 attempt exists; no timer state is created. |
[stderr] +| `TUT-FX-02` | From TUT-02 submit a configured typed alias, resolve, continue. | `TUT-02 → TUT-03`; outcome is the configured GAME-003 alias result and is not recomputed on continue. |
[stderr] +| `TUT-FX-03` | From TUT-03 submit an incorrect valid true/false value, resolve, continue. | `TUT-03 → TUT-04`; rejected text/non-colour feedback and canonical answer/explanation are recorded before continue. |
[stderr] +| `TUT-FX-04` | From TUT-04 submit its configured ordered pair, resolve, inspect explanation, continue. | `TUT-04 → TUT-05`; explanation availability is recorded; inspection does not change score, streak, or card position. |
[stderr] +| `TUT-FX-05` | Display TUT-05; `Pause`; restart; `Resume`; resolve; complete. | Pause snapshot has `activeCardId=TUT-05`, no unresolved answer, package `tutorial-v1`; restart restores that card; completion creates exactly one `first_whistle_complete` milestone and an immutable result. |
[stderr] +| `TUT-FX-06` | Repeat the completion command in TUT-FX-05 with the same completed-run ID and interaction ID. | Return the recorded completion/result; no second milestone, history entry, or score event is added. |
[stderr] +| `TUT-FX-07` | Start tutorial while offline with `tutorial-v1` cached; pause at TUT-05; restart while still offline. | Start, snapshot read, and resume succeed using cached package only; no network request is required. |
[stderr] +| `TUT-FX-08` | Start tutorial with no compatible cached tutorial package. | No run is created; show initial-content-required/retry/return-home state. It must not offer a substituted or partial tutorial. |
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## GPI-009 — Mixed Fixture selection
[stderr] +
[stderr] +`Mixed Fixture` starts with `(catalogueSnapshotId, selectionSeed, theme,
[stderr] +repeatLedger, timerMode)`. `theme` is either one selected category or
[stderr] +`kickoff_mix`; requested count is always ten. The selection first applies the
[stderr] +GAME-004 frozen-catalogue, publication, withdrawal, filter, anti-repeat, and
[stderr] +SHA-256 ordering policy. It then constructs the longest deterministic prefix
[stderr] +whose next card would not create a run of three equal `format` or three equal
[stderr] +`difficulty`. At each position, choose the first ranked candidate that keeps
[stderr] +both run lengths at two or fewer. If none does, choose the first ranked
[stderr] +candidate and append a variety-shortage record. This tie-free rule makes
[stderr] +selection reproducible and never rerolls.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +The saved selection contains selected card IDs/revisions, their frozen package
[stderr] +and rule versions, rank inputs, `selectionSeed`, timer mode, and both shortage
[stderr] +records. A shortage is displayed before start with the plain-language key
[stderr] +`selection_shortage_reuse_disclosed` (reuse/unfilled) and/or
[stderr] +`selection_shortage_variety_disclosed` (three-in-a-row unavoidable). A category
[stderr] +with no eligible cards does not create a run; it shows unavailable-category and
[stderr] +offers another eligible theme.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +### Seeded Mixed Fixture fixtures
[stderr] +
[stderr] +In these fixtures `ranked` is the ascending SHA-256 ordering already calculated
[stderr] +from the stated frozen snapshot and seed under GAME-004. Each token is
[stderr] +`ID:format:difficulty`; all candidates are published, in theme, and eligible
[stderr] +after the repeat policy unless a shortage field says otherwise.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +| ID | Snapshot / seed / ranked candidates | Expected selected IDs and records |
[stderr] +| --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] +| `MIX-FX-01` | `MF-1` / `north`; `A:S:1,B:T:2,C:O:3,D:S:2,E:T:1,F:O:2,G:S:3,H:T:1,I:O:2,J:S:1,K:T:3,L:O:1` | `A,B,C,D,E,F,G,H,I,J`; 10 fresh cards, no reuse/unfilled/variety shortage; every adjacent triple differs in both format and difficulty. |
[stderr] +| `MIX-FX-02` | `MF-2` / `west`; `A:S:1,B:S:2,C:S:3,D:T:1,E:O:2,F:T:3,G:O:1,H:S:2,I:T:1,J:O:3` | `A,B,D,C,E,F,G,H,I,J`; C moves after D because `A,B,C` would be three selects; no shortage. |
[stderr] +| `MIX-FX-03` | `MF-3` / `east`; `A:S:1,B:T:1,C:O:1,D:S:2,E:T:2,F:O:2,G:S:3,H:T:3,I:O:3,J:S:1` | `A,B,D,C,E,F,G,H,I,J`; D moves before C because the first three ranked cards share difficulty 1; no shortage. |
[stderr] +| `MIX-FX-04` | `MF-4` / `south`; `A:S:1,B:S:2,C:S:3,D:S:1,E:S:2,F:S:3,G:S:1,H:S:2,I:S:3,J:S:1` | `A,B,C,D,E,F,G,H,I,J`; formats have no alternative, so record format variety shortages at positions 3–10 with `selection_shortage_variety_disclosed` before start. |
[stderr] +| `MIX-FX-05` | `MF-5` / `cup`; fresh ranked `A:S:1,B:T:2,C:O:3,D:S:2,E:T:1,F:O:2,G:S:3,H:T:2`, then reused ranked `I:O:3,J:S:1`; requested 10 | Select A–H then I,J; record reused IDs I,J and `selection_shortage_reuse_disclosed`; variety rule is still evaluated over the final order. |
[stderr] +| `MIX-FX-06` | `MF-6` / `cup`; seven eligible ranked `A:S:1,B:T:2,C:O:3,D:S:2,E:T:1,F:O:2,G:S:3`; requested 10 | Select A–G only; record `requestedCount=10`, `eligibleAvailable=7`, `unfilledCount=3`, and `selection_shortage_reuse_disclosed`; do not pad with unpublished, withdrawn, or invented cards. |
[stderr] +| `MIX-FX-07` | `MF-7` / `empty-theme`; no eligible candidates | No run/snapshot; show unavailable-category and eligible-theme choice. |
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Optional timer and round lifecycle
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Timer is an accessibility-neutral optional display mode: `off` is the default
[stderr] +and tutorial always forces `off`. Starting a standard round freezes the chosen
[stderr] +mode. `on` records elapsed active seconds only; it does not change selection,
[stderr] +adjudication, score, streak, or availability. Pause, background interruption,
[stderr] +and recovery stop elapsed time. A timeout can be emitted only for an explicitly
[stderr] +enabled timer according to the separately implemented GAME-007 scoring rule.
[stderr] +
